DATA={
'98858':dict(name='io_uring SQPOLL task-work use-after-free',files=['io_uring/io_uring.c','io_uring/sqpoll.c'],
primitive='Publishing the final request to the SQPOLL task-work list can let the polling thread complete it and free ctx/tctx before io_req_normal_work_add finishes using them. The primary report contains both a four-byte freed-object read and an eight-byte freed-object write. The fix holds an RCU read section across publication and waits for a grace period for SQPOLL ring destruction.',
gates='CONFIG_IO_URING=y in the exact archived .95 build. io_uring_allowed() permits ordinary callers at kernel.io_uring_disabled=0; value1 requires initial-userns CAP_SYS_ADMIN or membership in the configured initial-userns group; value2 blocks new setup. io_sq_offload_create() also invokes security_uring_sqpoll(). There is no unconditional host-capability requirement for SQPOLL. Existing rings, LSM state and actual sysctl policy remain runtime predicates. Both disabled values1/2 are reviewed values, not automatic safe rules in the evaluator.',
current='The .113 io_req_normal_work_add RCU guard and io_ring_exit_work SQPOLL grace-period condition match stable42b3332e. The source correction is present; source inclusion alone does not establish which release a node booted.',
en='An ordinary VPS process can race task-work submission and teardown of an io_uring ring using submission polling, when node policy permits that interface. The shared kernel can access ring state after it has been freed, including a reported write through a freed object. This makes root access inside the VPS plausible; a more advanced exploit could potentially gain control of the node or access another VPS, but the reviewed upstream report and fix do not establish either outcome on this platform. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel.',
cs='Běžný proces ve VPS může vyvolat souběh předávání úloh a rušení io_uring fronty s pollingem, pokud toto rozhraní povoluje politika node. Sdílené jádro pak může přistupovat k již uvolněným datům fronty; hlášen byl i zápis přes uvolněný objekt. Chyba tak může umožnit získání práv root ve VPS. Pokročilejší zneužití by mohlo vést k ovládnutí node nebo přístupu do jiného VPS, ale analyzované upstreamové hlášení a oprava takový výsledek na této platformě nedokládají. Neúspěšný pokus může shodit sdílené jádro.'),
'98260':dict(name='POSIX CPU timer cleanup after failed exec',files=['fs/exec.c','kernel/time/posix-cpu-timers.c'],
primitive='A nonleader exec changes TID ownership in de_thread. A still-queued per-thread CPU timer can lose the PID lookup that would unlink it. A later exec failure after point_of_no_return reaches exit_itimers before posix_cpu_timers_exit, freeing a queued k_itimer; reaping then erases the freed rb-tree node. The fix moves POSIX timer cleanup immediately after de_thread, before later failure points.',
gates='CONFIG_POSIX_TIMERS=y in the exact archived build. A process can create its own thread CPU timer and control its own threads, exec lifecycle and parent reaping. No host capability, device or optional module is required. The default seccomp profile does not deny the timer, exec or wait syscalls. The failure point and lifetime race remain necessary; ordinary successful exec is not sufficient.',
current='The .113 begin_new_exec calls posixtimer_exec directly after successful de_thread, matching stable d9ae467e. This is distinct from published CVE-2026-64560 and its deletion/adjustment race; that older correction does not prove this later failed-exec case fixed.',
en='An ordinary multithreaded VPS process can leave a POSIX CPU timer queued while a non-leading thread replaces its program and that operation fails. The shared kernel can later manipulate the timer after freeing it. The resulting memory corruption makes root access inside the VPS plausible. A more advanced exploit could potentially gain control of the node or access another VPS, but the reviewed upstream report and fix do not establish either outcome on this platform. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel.',
cs='Běžný vícevláknový proces ve VPS může ponechat POSIX CPU časovač ve frontě, pokud jiné než vedoucí vlákno nahrazuje svůj program a tato operace selže. Sdílené jádro pak může s časovačem pracovat i po jeho uvolnění. Následné poškození paměti může umožnit získání práv root ve VPS. Pokročilejší zneužití by mohlo vést k ovládnutí node nebo přístupu do jiného VPS, ale analyzované upstreamové hlášení a oprava takový výsledek na této platformě nedokládají. Neúspěšný pokus může shodit sdílené jádro.'),
'97594':dict(name='Landlock source-parent dentry use-after-free',files=['security/landlock/fs.c','security/landlock/syscalls.c','security/landlock/setup.c'],
primitive='current_check_refer_path used old_dentry->d_parent without a reference or lock. linkat does not have the rename-path lock that protects hook_path_rename. Concurrent rename/rmdir can release that parent while Landlock walks its hierarchy. The fix uses dget/dget_parent and balances dput after checks and any synchronous audit. The primary KASAN report establishes a freed dentry read; arbitrary writes/control flow are not demonstrated by that report.',
gates='CONFIG_SECURITY_LANDLOCK=y and the compiled CONFIG_LSM list starts with landlock in the exact .95 build. It is therefore not a compiled-subsystem exclusion. landlock_restrict_self permits self-confinement with no_new_privs; no host capability is required. The process must enter a domain handling at least one filesystem right, then operate on its own link/rename/remove paths. Active LSM ordering or boot lsm= can change runtime availability and is not a generic schema predicate.',
current='The .113 current_check_refer_path pins old_parent via dget/dget_parent and releases it on exit, matching stable4c37992b. No historical current-LSM identity is inferred from the compiled list.',
en='When Landlock is active, an ordinary VPS process can enter its own filesystem restriction domain and race hard-link creation against directory moves and removal. The shared kernel can read a directory object after it has been freed. Further exploitation might gain root inside the VPS or affect the node and other VPSes, but the reviewed upstream report demonstrates a freed-object access rather than a complete privilege-escalation or isolation-bypass exploit. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel.',
cs='Pokud je Landlock aktivní, běžný proces ve VPS si může nastavit vlastní omezení souborového systému a souběžně vytvářet pevné odkazy, přesouvat adresáře a odstraňovat je. Sdílené jádro pak může číst již uvolněný objekt adresáře. Další zneužití by mohlo vést k získání práv root ve VPS nebo ohrozit node a ostatní VPS, ale analyzované upstreamové hlášení dokládá přístup k uvolněnému objektu, nikoli úplné zneužití ke zvýšení oprávnění nebo prolomení izolace. Neúspěšný pokus může shodit sdílené jádro.',impact=['possible','possible','possible','plausible']),
'80521':dict(name='AF_UNIX garbage-collector SCC use-after-free',files=['net/unix/garbage.c'],
primitive='An SCM_RIGHTS send can publish a graph edge before its skb is queued. Concurrent closes let garbage collection partly free a strongly connected component while a surviving vertex retains scc_entry pointing at a freed vertex. The next fast SCC walk follows that stale link. The fix unlinks scc_entry when unix_del_edge removes the final outgoing edge. List traversal/collection through reclaimed vertices supplies a plausible corruption primitive, not a platform exploit demonstration.',
gates='CONFIG_UNIX=y in the exact archived build. Ordinary AF_UNIX sockets, SCM_RIGHTS send and close suffice; no network-administration capability or delegated physical device is required. The tenant controls its own socket cycles. The default seccomp denylist does not prohibit these operations. Namespace isolation does not create a separate kernel allocator for the graph objects.',
current='The .113 unix_del_edge includes list_del(&vertex->scc_entry), matching1293fd69. Primary explicit backport introductions6.1.141/6.6.93 override the global6.10 introduction for those older branches.',
en='An ordinary VPS process can race passing UNIX socket descriptors against closing sockets in a cyclic reference graph. The UNIX socket garbage collector can then follow a link to an object it has already freed. This makes root access inside the VPS plausible; a more advanced exploit could potentially gain control of the node or access another VPS. The reviewed upstream report and fix do not establish either isolation outcome on this platform. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel.',
cs='Běžný proces ve VPS může souběžně předávat deskriptory unixových socketů a zavírat sockety propojené cyklickými odkazy. Úklid nepoužívaných unixových socketů pak může následovat odkaz na již uvolněný objekt. Chyba tak může umožnit získání práv root ve VPS. Pokročilejší zneužití by mohlo vést k ovládnutí node nebo přístupu do jiného VPS. Analyzované upstreamové hlášení a oprava takové prolomení izolace na této platformě nedokládají. Neúspěšný pokus může shodit sdílené jádro.'),
'53388':dict(name='FUSE splice request use-after-free',files=['fs/fuse/dev.c','fs/fuse/inode.c'],
primitive='fuse_try_move_folio unlocks the request but originally did not lock it again on successful page replacement. fuse_chan_abort can then finish the request and free fuse_io_args while subsequent copying still uses it. The stable correction locks the request before replacing the page-cache folio, preventing abort from freeing the arguments during the later copy. Older branches use the equivalent page helper.',
gates='CONFIG_FUSE_FS=m in the archived build; vpsAdminOS explicitly preloads fuse. vpsAdmin defaults the FUSE feature on and delegates char10:229 /dev/fuse. Downstream FUSE filesystem registration includes FS_USERNS_MOUNT; tenant userns administration can mount it and control its daemon. Per-VPS feature/device permissions and actual module availability remain runtime facts. Default seccomp does not deny the needed mount/splice operations.',
current='The inclusive range starts at.95: stable46473ddc is first released in6.12.95 and the archived .95 source already includes lock_request before folio replacement. Current .113 retains it. A booted unmodified .95 is source-fixed for this CVE; an old FUSE livepatch tuple is neither needed for that release conclusion nor copied into this dossier.',
en='On an affected kernel, a VPS process with access to a FUSE mount and its userspace filesystem server can race page transfer against request cancellation. The shared kernel may use request arguments after they have been freed. This makes root access inside the VPS plausible; a more advanced exploit could potentially gain control of the node or access another VPS, but the reviewed upstream report and fix do not establish either outcome on this platform. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel.',
cs='Na zranitelném jádře může proces ve VPS s přístupem k připojenému FUSE a jeho uživatelskému serveru souběžně přenášet stránky a rušit požadavky. Sdílené jádro pak může používat argumenty požadavku i po jejich uvolnění. Chyba tak může umožnit získání práv root ve VPS. Pokročilejší zneužití by mohlo vést k ovládnutí node nebo přístupu do jiného VPS, ale analyzované upstreamové hlášení a oprava takový výsledek na této platformě nedokládají. Neúspěšný pokus může shodit sdílené jádro.')}
DATA.update({
'63824':dict(name='Asymmetric keyctl output-buffer overflow',files=['security/keys/keyctl_pkey.c','crypto/asymmetric_keys/asymmetric_type.c'],
primitive='keyctl_pkey_params_get_2 sized an internal output buffer from the caller-provided short out_len, although the selected asymmetric cryptographic operation can emit its full primitive output. The fix sizes output from queried max_enc_size/max_dec_size/max_sig_size for the chosen operation. This is kernel heap overflow, not merely truncation of the user result.',
gates='The exact archived build has KEYS, ASYMMETRIC_KEY_TYPE, ASYMMETRIC_PUBLIC_KEY_SUBTYPE, X509_CERTIFICATE_PARSER and CRYPTO_RSA built in. A process can create/search its own keyring and import an asymmetric public key. A public-key encryption route does not require the separately modular PKCS8 private-key parser. Default seccomp allows keyctl; key permissions and LSM policy still apply. No blanket privileged-module prerequisite is justified for this public-key route.',
current='Current .113 keyctl_pkey_params_get_2 assigns params->out_len from the primitive maxima before allocation, matching6.12 stable5165f1cc. The fix is already included in .95; it does not rely on an unverified livepatch.',
en='On an affected kernel, an ordinary VPS process with a usable asymmetric key can request a cryptographic operation with an undersized output buffer. The kernel can allocate too little memory and overwrite adjacent data. This makes root access inside the VPS plausible; a more advanced exploit could potentially gain control of the node or access another VPS, but the reviewed upstream report and fix do not establish either outcome on this platform. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel.',
cs='Na zranitelném jádře může běžný proces ve VPS s použitelným asymetrickým klíčem požádat o kryptografickou operaci s příliš malým výstupním bufferem. Jádro pak může vyhradit málo paměti a přepsat okolní data. Chyba tak může umožnit získání práv root ve VPS. Pokročilejší zneužití by mohlo vést k ovládnutí node nebo přístupu do jiného VPS, ale analyzované upstreamové hlášení a oprava takový výsledek na této platformě nedokládají. Neúspěšný pokus může shodit sdílené jádro.'),
'74753':dict(name='perf EXIT group-leader use-after-free',files=['kernel/events/core.c'],
primitive='remove_on_exec detaches a perf group and puts its leader in EXIT, while its descriptor can stay open. Accepting a new sibling under that detached leader leaves a stale group_leader pointer when the leader closes because the attach bit is already clear. The fix rejects EXIT leaders both early and under the shared context mutex. The earlier detach-on-exec correction introduced this regression; .95 predates the6.12.96 introduction.',
gates='CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS=y in the exact archived build. kernel.perf_event_paranoid=2 prohibits unprivileged kernel tracing and CPU-wide events but permits a process own per-task userspace event with exclude_kernel and appropriate sample flags. A software event is sufficient for the group lifecycle; no IntelPT hardware is needed for this CVE. Default seccomp permits perf_event_open; LSM restrictions remain runtime policy.',
current='Current .113 perf_event_open rejects group_leader->state<=PERF_EVENT_STATE_EXIT before and after taking the context mutex, matchinge593031f. Mainline introduction037a3c43 has Makefile7.2.0-rc1 and correctionfa091f46 precedes final7.2. The exact global interval is rc1..final, while stable ranges are explicitly .96–.107 on6.12. The existing evaluator strips release-candidate suffixes: actual7.2 RC/custom releases must be flagged by the shared snapshot gate and escalated, never hand-classified or replaced with an invented released mainline interval.',
en='On affected kernels, an ordinary VPS process can attach a new performance-event sibling to a group leader that has already exited during program replacement. Closing that leader can leave the sibling pointing to freed kernel memory. This makes root access inside the VPS plausible; a more advanced exploit could potentially gain control of the node or access another VPS, but the reviewed upstream report and fix do not establish either outcome on this platform. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel.',
cs='Na zranitelném jádře může běžný proces ve VPS připojit další událost měření výkonu k vedoucí události skupiny, která již při nahrazení programu přešla do ukončeného stavu. Po zavření vedoucí události může další událost stále odkazovat na uvolněnou paměť jádra. Chyba tak může umožnit získání práv root ve VPS. Pokročilejší zneužití by mohlo vést k ovládnutí node nebo přístupu do jiného VPS, ale analyzované upstreamové hlášení a oprava takový výsledek na této platformě nedokládají. Neúspěšný pokus může shodit sdílené jádro.'),
'93817':dict(name='perf address-filter lifetime use-after-free',files=['kernel/events/core.c','arch/x86/events/intel/pt.c','arch/x86/events/intel/Makefile'],
primitive='perf event addr_filter_ranges is read under RCU, but __free_event freed it immediately before readers had completed. Moving kfree to free_event_rcu preserves its lifetime through the grace period. The primary description is narrow and supplies no end-to-end exploit; downstream inherited-event/address-filter paths establish the relevant dangling-array read/copy lifetime.',
gates='PERF_EVENTS=y and CPU_SUP_INTEL=y in the exact archived build. The Intel events Makefile builds pt.o under CPU_SUP_INTEL; there is no fabricated CONFIG_INTEL_PT requirement. Actual Intel Processor Trace PMU/hardware and address-filter support are necessary for the identified platform path. Per-task userspace exclude_kernel events are not prohibited by paranoid2 alone, but LSM, CPU and PMU availability remain unmodeled runtime predicates. Own inheritance/exec/mmap and filter updates provide the relevant lifetime operations.',
current='Current .113 moves kfree(event->addr_filter_ranges) into free_event_rcu and no longer frees it early in __free_event, matchingcd8dab11. Compiler support for Intel CPUs does not establish the actual PMU of every node.',
en='On hardware providing the affected processor-trace address filters, an ordinary VPS process allowed to create its own performance events can race their lifetime against filter use. The shared kernel can access a freed filter array. Further exploitation could potentially gain root inside the VPS, affect the node or access another VPS, but the reviewed upstream report and source establish the lifetime error rather than a complete escalation or isolation-bypass exploit. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel.',
cs='Na hardwaru s dotčenými adresními filtry trasování procesoru může běžný proces ve VPS, který smí vytvářet vlastní události měření výkonu, vyvolat souběh jejich rušení a používání filtrů. Sdílené jádro pak může přistupovat k uvolněnému poli filtrů. Další zneužití by mohlo vést k získání práv root ve VPS, ohrozit node nebo umožnit přístup do jiného VPS, ale analyzované upstreamové hlášení a zdrojový kód dokládají chybu životnosti objektu, nikoli úplné zvýšení oprávnění nebo prolomení izolace. Neúspěšný pokus může shodit sdílené jádro.',impact=['possible','possible','possible','plausible']),
'74517':dict(name='KVM delayed IOAPIC EOI vCPU use-after-free',files=['arch/x86/kvm/x86.c','arch/x86/kvm/ioapic.c'],
primitive='Delayed I/O APIC EOI injection can try to deliver an IRQ to vCPUs after VM teardown has freed them. The fix cancels and flushes eoi_inject in kvm_arch_pre_destroy_vm, before vCPU destruction, while retaining VM interrupt-controller state until its normal destruction. Primary KASAN establishes an eight-byte stale vCPU access; it does not demonstrate host-root control.',
gates='CONFIG_KVM=m in the exact archived build; vpsAdmin defaults KVM on and delegates /dev/kvm. A tenant VMM with device permission can create/run its own VM and in-kernel IRQchip and trigger teardown. Vendor module availability and virtualization CPU support remain actual runtime prerequisites; no nested VMX requirement is imposed for this vendor-independent x86 path. Ordinary tenant root is not initial-userns host root.',
current='The .113 kvm_arch_pre_destroy_vm cancels delayed IOAPIC work before kvm_mmu_pre_destroy_vm, matching69d04044. CNA explicitly introduces the older6.12 branch at6.12.41 via c60f5156, despite global6.14 introduction. Both are recorded instead of incorrectly marking6.12 safe by its major/minor age.',
en='A VPS process with access to KVM can race shutdown of its virtual machine against delayed virtual interrupt handling. The shared kernel can then access a virtual CPU after it has been freed. Further exploitation could potentially gain root inside the VPS, take control of the node or access another VPS, but the reviewed upstream report and fix demonstrate the freed-object access rather than a complete guest-to-host exploit. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel.',
cs='Proces ve VPS s přístupem ke KVM může vyvolat souběh ukončování svého virtuálního stroje a odloženého zpracování virtuálního přerušení. Sdílené jádro pak může přistupovat k již uvolněnému virtuálnímu CPU. Další zneužití by mohlo vést k získání práv root ve VPS, ovládnutí node nebo přístupu do jiného VPS, ale analyzované upstreamové hlášení a oprava dokládají přístup k uvolněnému objektu, nikoli úplné zneužití k úniku z virtuálního stroje. Neúspěšný pokus může shodit sdílené jádro.',impact=['possible','possible','possible','plausible']),
'89929':dict(name='KVM nested INVVPID wrong-CPU stale translations',files=['arch/x86/kvm/vmx/nested.c','arch/x86/kvm/vmx/vmx.c'],
primitive='Nested INVVPID emulation could invalidate vpid02 on a different physical CPU than the one on which L2 last ran. Migration back left stale TLB mappings valid. The fix pins the CPU while checking vmcs02.cpu and clears last_vpid when a deferred flush on the correct CPU is needed. This establishes nested translation-isolation risk, not unrestricted L0 arbitrary memory access.',
gates='KVM=m and KVM_INTEL=m in the exact archived build. Default KVM device delegation lets a tenant VMM expose nested VMX. kvm_intel nested=1 and vpid=1 are source defaults, not measured parameters. Intel VMX/VPID CPU support, actual vendor module, nested guest exposure and a nested invalidation/migration sequence are necessary. An AMD-only node would not take this Intel path; CONFIG_KVM_INTEL=m alone cannot prove actual exposure.',
current='Current .113 handle_invvpid uses get_cpu, compares the last vmcs02 CPU, invalidates last_vpid on mismatch and calls put_cpu, matchingd03e7218. No deployed CPU/module/default identity is inferred from these sources.',
en='On Intel KVM with nested virtualization and tagged translations enabled, a VPS virtual-machine monitor can exercise an invalidation path that leaves stale memory translations on another CPU. This can break isolation between nested guest mappings. The reviewed upstream report and source do not establish root access inside the VPS, control of the node or access to another VPS; those broader outcomes require a separate exploit path. Stale mappings can corrupt a guest or disrupt its operation.',
cs='Při použití Intel KVM se zapnutou vnořenou virtualizací a označovanými překlady adres může monitor virtuálního stroje ve VPS vyvolat cestu invalidace, která na jiném CPU ponechá staré překlady paměti. Tím může být narušena izolace mapování vnořeného hosta. Analyzované upstreamové hlášení a zdrojový kód nedokládají získání práv root ve VPS, ovládnutí node ani přístup do jiného VPS; takové širší dopady vyžadují další postup zneužití. Staré mapování může poškodit paměť hosta nebo narušit jeho provoz.',summary_en='Nested virtualization isolation failure',summary_cs='Narušení izolace vnořené virtualizace',impact=['unlikely','possible','possible','possible'],warning=False,
outcomes='The concrete primitive is stale nested-guest translation use after incomplete invalidation. Nested L1/L2 isolation can fail, but a tenant-controllable nested mapping is not automatically arbitrary L0 host physical memory. VPS-root escalation is unlikely from the reviewed direct mechanism; node-root/cross-VPS and node-availability consequences remain possible without an established complete platform exploit. Primary CVSS claims, if present, remain separate from this outcome assessment.')})
DATA.update({
'89930':dict(name='KVM failed nested VM-entry stale TLB',files=['arch/x86/kvm/vmx/nested.c','arch/x86/kvm/vmx/vmx.c'],
primitive='A failed nested VM-entry updated last_vpid or queued local TLB flushes after switching to L2 context without servicing those flushes. A following successful entry could then reuse stale mappings. The fix services kvm_service_local_tlb_flush_requests in vmentry_fail_vmexit_guest_mode before leave_guest_mode. This concerns nested address-translation semantics, not an arbitrary host write demonstrated in the primary record.',
gates='KVM and KVM_INTEL are modular in the exact archived build. vpsAdmin KVM defaults on and delegates /dev/kvm. A tenant VMM may expose nested Intel VMX; actual Intel hardware, vendor module, nested exposure and transition controls are runtime requirements. Source nested=1/VPID defaults do not prove observed node settings. The identified trigger is a failed then successful nested entry with pending invalidation/VPID tracking, not ordinary guest traffic.',
current='The .113 failed nested VM-entry path calls kvm_service_local_tlb_flush_requests before leaving guest mode, matchingf74fccdf. The correction complements89929/89932 but is an independently assigned defect.',
en='On Intel KVM with nested virtualization, a failed entry into a nested guest can leave a required memory-translation invalidation pending. A later successful entry can use stale mappings and break nested guest isolation. The reviewed upstream report and source do not establish root access inside the VPS, control of the node or access to another VPS; those broader outcomes require a separate exploit path. Stale mappings can corrupt a guest or disrupt its operation.',
cs='Při použití Intel KVM s vnořenou virtualizací může po neúspěšném vstupu do vnořeného hosta zůstat neprovedená požadovaná invalidace překladů paměti. Pozdější úspěšný vstup pak může použít stará mapování a narušit izolaci vnořeného hosta. Analyzované upstreamové hlášení a zdrojový kód nedokládají získání práv root ve VPS, ovládnutí node ani přístup do jiného VPS; takové širší dopady vyžadují další postup zneužití. Staré mapování může poškodit paměť hosta nebo narušit jeho provoz.',summary_en='Nested virtualization isolation failure',summary_cs='Narušení izolace vnořené virtualizace',impact=['unlikely','possible','possible','possible'],warning=False,
outcomes='The source establishes stale nested translations after a failed entry, with potential nested isolation failure. A guest physical mapping is not automatically arbitrary L0 physical memory. VPS-root is unlikely from this direct mechanism; node-root, cross-VPS and node availability remain possible rather than demonstrated on the platform.'),
'89932':dict(name='KVM nested VPID reuse across VM lifetimes',files=['arch/x86/kvm/vmx/nested.c','arch/x86/kvm/vmx/vmx.c'],
primitive='last_vpid was initialized only at vCPU creation, not when VMXOFF released vpid02 and VMXON later allocated it again. Reusing a VPID with translations from an earlier vCPU or completely different VM could let the new L2 use those stale translations. The fix resets last_vpid=0 at allocation so the first nested entry forces invalidation. The explicit prior-VM lifetime supplies a concrete cross-VM mapping mechanism; attacker control of placement/reuse and reliable access remain qualifications.',
gates='KVM/KVM_INTEL=m in the exact archived build, default delegated /dev/kvm, Intel VMX with VPID and nested exposure are necessary. The source defaults nested=1 and vpid=1 are not deployment proof. The tenant VMM or its L1 controls VMXOFF/VMXON/L2 lifetime; physical CPU scheduling and VPID reuse determine whether a previous VM translation survives. No separate operator-only nested feature is inferred.',
current='The .113 enter_vmx_operation resets last_vpid immediately after allocate_vpid, matching8b98d662. This is the strongest of the three stale-TLB reports for another-VM relevance, but the actual source does not demonstrate exploitation across two vpsFree VPSes.',
en='On Intel KVM with nested virtualization and tagged translations enabled, restarting nested virtualization can reuse translations retained from an earlier virtual CPU or even a different virtual machine. This creates a plausible route to reading or modifying another virtual machine’s memory if the required reuse occurs. The reviewed upstream report and source do not establish root access inside the VPS or complete control of the node, and they do not demonstrate an attack between two VPSes on this platform. Corrupted guest memory can disrupt operation.',
cs='Při použití Intel KVM se zapnutou vnořenou virtualizací a označovanými překlady adres může opětovné spuštění vnořené virtualizace použít překlady ponechané po dřívějším virtuálním CPU nebo i jiném virtuálním stroji. Pokud nastane potřebné opětovné použití identifikátoru, vzniká tím reálná možnost čtení nebo změny paměti jiného virtuálního stroje. Analyzované upstreamové hlášení a zdrojový kód nedokládají získání práv root ve VPS ani úplné ovládnutí node a nepopisují útok mezi dvěma VPS na této platformě. Poškození paměti hosta může narušit jeho provoz.',summary_en='Cross-VM memory isolation failure',summary_cs='Narušení izolace paměti virtuálních strojů',impact=['unlikely','possible','plausible','possible'],warning=False,
outcomes='Cross-VM memory access is plausible because the primary fix explicitly names stale entries from a completely different VM lifetime. Mapping reuse is a mechanism, not a reproduced vpsFree cross-VPS attack. Arbitrary host-root control remains possible without a complete demonstrated path; no direct credential-root mechanism is established.'),
'98720':dict(name='KVM enlightened nested TPR isolation bypass',files=['arch/x86/kvm/vmx/nested.c','arch/x86/kvm/vmx/hyperv.c','arch/x86/kvm/x86.c'],
primitive='Changing runtime enlightened-VMCS controls did not force refresh of the nested MSR bitmap. Switching TPR virtualization off after L2 had run with it on could retain TPR passthrough, allowing L2 or L1 by proxy to read/write L0 TPR. The fix sets force_msr_bitmap_recalc when runtime control groups are dirty. Access to the host task-priority register is an explicit L0 boundary violation, not proof of arbitrary host memory/root control.',
gates='KVM/KVM_INTEL=m and KVM_HYPERV=y in the exact archived build. A delegated tenant VMM can enable KVM_CAP_HYPERV_ENLIGHTENED_VMCS through ordinary KVM_ENABLE_CAP when supported; this is guest eVMCS support, distinct from host-under-Hyper-V enlightened acceleration. Intel VMX/nested/eVMCS availability, relevant enlightened MSR bitmap feature and TPR control sequence remain runtime/guest prerequisites. Device policy and source nested defaults are not observed hardware proof.',
current='The .113 copy_enlightened_to_vmcs12 tests runtime control clean bits and forces MSR-bitmap recalculation, matching2db11598. The code preserves the difference between guest eVMCS capability and host Hyper-V environment.',
en='On Intel KVM with the affected enlightened nested-virtualization interface enabled, changing virtual interrupt controls can leave an outdated register-access bitmap. A nested guest can then read or write the node’s task-priority register. The reviewed upstream report establishes this host-register boundary violation, but it does not establish root access inside the VPS, arbitrary node control or access to another VPS. Changing host interrupt priority can disrupt execution.',
cs='Při použití Intel KVM se zapnutým dotčeným rozhraním enlightened vnořené virtualizace může změna řízení virtuálních přerušení ponechat zastaralou bitmapu přístupu k registrům. Vnořený host pak může číst nebo zapisovat registr priority úloh na node. Analyzované upstreamové hlášení dokládá překročení hranice přístupu k registru hostitele, nikoli získání práv root ve VPS, libovolné ovládnutí node nebo přístup do jiného VPS. Změna priority přerušení hostitele může narušit běh systému.',summary_en='Nested virtualization isolation bypass',summary_cs='Obejití izolace vnořené virtualizace',impact=['unlikely','possible','possible','plausible'],warning=False,
outcomes='The primary report explicitly establishes L0 TPR read/write through the faulty nested controls. Node availability is plausible from host interrupt-priority effects. Arbitrary node-root/kernel-code execution and cross-VPS access are possible extensions, not demonstrated by this register-level primitive; VPS-root escalation is not the direct mechanism.'),
'63830':dict(name='SK_MSG BPF scatterlist ownership corruption',files=['net/core/skmsg.c','net/core/filter.c','kernel/bpf/syscall.c','kernel/bpf/token.c','include/linux/bpf.h'],
primitive='Scatterlist transforms moved SG entries without their sg.copy ownership bits. An externally backed entry such as a spliced file-page-cache page could then be exposed as writable SK_MSG ctx->data, allowing BPF stores to modify original page-cache bytes. The fix propagates/clears ownership through pull/push/pop/shift/xfer and TLS record splitting. The primitive is unauthorised backing-page modification, distinct from ordinary writable packet data.',
gates='BPF_SYSCALL=y and NET_SOCK_MSG=y in the exact archived build. Current6.12 source sets unprivileged_bpf_disabled=0, but SK_MSG is a privileged program type: bpf_prog_load requires CAP_BPF and its network-type CAP_NET_ADMIN through bpf_token_capable. Without a token, those are initial-userns capability checks; tenant userns capabilities alone are insufficient. A valid token requires deliberately delegated bpffs policy, commands, program/attach types and its userns capability. No such tenant delegation is established by this source review. An installed privileged SK_MSG path and suitable external page/transform are alternative runtime conditions; unprivileged socket-filter availability alone is not the trigger.',
current='The .113 skmsg/filter ownership transformations carry sg.copy bits, matching stable d22cc92b. Source fixes are already present in .95. The capability/token gates remain relevant when assessing older releases.',
en='On an affected kernel, a specially arranged SK_MSG BPF program can make file-backed memory appear writable and change the underlying page cache. Loading this program requires BPF and network-administration authority that VPS user-namespace capabilities alone do not grant, or an explicitly delegated BPF token. If that prerequisite is met, the write primitive makes privilege escalation and shared-file corruption plausible; the reviewed upstream report and source do not establish a complete node-control or cross-VPS exploit. Corruption can also disrupt workloads.',
cs='Na zranitelném jádře může speciálně sestavený program SK_MSG BPF zpřístupnit paměť podloženou souborem pro zápis a změnit příslušnou stránkovou cache. Načtení tohoto programu vyžaduje oprávnění k BPF a správě sítě, která samotné capabilities v uživatelském jmenném prostoru VPS neposkytují, nebo výslovně delegovaný BPF token. Při splnění této podmínky může zápis umožnit zvýšení oprávnění a poškození sdílených souborů. Analyzované upstreamové hlášení a zdrojový kód nedokládají úplný postup k ovládnutí node ani zneužití mezi VPS. Poškození může také narušit běh aplikací.',impact=['possible','possible','possible','possible'],warning=False,
outcomes='The page-cache write primitive can subvert file integrity and plausibly support privilege escalation when privileged SK_MSG authority or an installed reachable program exists. Ordinary VPS processes lack that initial-userns program authority under the reviewed profile. This is a scoped source-profile gate, not fleet-wide historical proof or an evaluator safe override. Cross-VPS impact additionally depends on shared backing-page scope; ordinary tenant-private files do not alone establish another VPS target.'),
'74616':dict(name='XDP broadcast clone shared-info overlap',files=['net/core/xdp.c','kernel/bpf/syscall.c','kernel/bpf/token.c'],
primitive='xdpf_clone copied linear frame contents into one page and checked only PAGE_SIZE, omitting skb_shared_info tailroom. A larger original frame could fit that check yet overlap shared-info when converted back to skb; later writes corrupt XDP return metadata. The fix limits the clone to SKB_WITH_OVERHEAD(PAGE_SIZE).',
gates='BPF_SYSCALL=y in the exact archived build. XDP broadcast redirect/clone plus XDP-to-skb conversion and a source allocation large enough to hit tailroom are necessary. Loading XDP is privileged: CAP_BPF and CAP_NET_ADMIN via initial-userns checks without an explicitly delegated valid BPF token. Ordinary namespace NET_ADMIN alone does not authorize this program type. An operator-installed affected XDP path could expose packet-driven processing, but no actual program/device path is established by source defaults or ordinary traffic alone. unprivileged_bpf_disabled=0 does not grant privileged XDP authority.',
current='The .113 xdpf_clone checks totalsize>SKB_WITH_OVERHEAD(PAGE_SIZE), matchingef4b7c70. A compiled BPF syscall or current source default is insufficient to establish an installed vulnerable XDP broadcast program.',
en='On an affected kernel, an XDP broadcast-copy path can place packet bytes over bookkeeping used when the copy becomes a normal network packet. Later processing can corrupt kernel metadata. Loading XDP requires BPF and network-administration authority that VPS user-namespace capabilities alone do not grant, or an explicitly delegated BPF token; an already installed affected program is another material prerequisite. With that path available, privilege escalation or damage to the shared node is possible, but the reviewed upstream report and fix do not establish a complete node-control or cross-VPS exploit. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel.',
cs='Na zranitelném jádře může cesta vytváření broadcastových kopií XDP umístit data paketu přes pomocná data používaná při převodu kopie na běžný síťový paket. Další zpracování pak může poškodit metadata jádra. Načtení XDP vyžaduje oprávnění k BPF a správě sítě, která samotné capabilities v uživatelském jmenném prostoru VPS neposkytují, nebo výslovně delegovaný BPF token; další podstatnou podmínkou je případný již nainstalovaný dotčený program. Při dostupnosti této cesty je možné zvýšení oprávnění nebo poškození sdíleného node, ale analyzované upstreamové hlášení a oprava nedokládají úplný postup k ovládnutí node ani zneužití mezi VPS. Neúspěšný pokus může shodit sdílené jádro.',impact=['possible','possible','possible','plausible'])})
DATA.update({
'98039':dict(name='BPF per-CPU kptr type confusion',files=['kernel/bpf/verifier.c','kernel/bpf/syscall.c','kernel/bpf/token.c'],
primitive='map_kptr_match_type allowed a plain allocated object or referenced kernel pointer in a BPF_KPTR_PERCPU field because the allowed-flags subset check did not require MEM_PERCPU. A later field load always adds MEM_PERCPU, so per-CPU pointer relocation and teardown interpret an ordinary pointer as a per-CPU allocation cookie. The primary fix explicitly identifies arbitrary kernel read/write for a plain allocation, with invalid relocation or missing-destructor paths for kernel pointers. The fix requires source MEM_PERCPU to match the destination field kind.',
gates='CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL=y in the archived build. The primitive needs a BTF kptr-capable map and program/kfunc access to the object allocation/per-CPU helpers; it is not established for a plain unprivileged socket-filter program. BTF loading requires bpf_token_capable(CAP_BPF), and eligible program types/kfunc sets, JIT and kernel BTF are further gates. Without deliberate valid token delegation, the relevant capability is initial-userns, not tenant userns. Current unprivileged_bpf_disabled=0 permits some BPF but does not confer these authorities. Actual delegated program/token/installed path remains unmeasured.',
current='The .113 map_kptr_match_type explicitly compares BPF_KPTR_PERCPU against the source MEM_PERCPU flag, matchingaaa9cf77. No reviewed source default establishes token delegation to a VPS.',
en='On an affected kernel, a BPF program with the required typed-map and kernel-function access can store an ordinary pointer where the verifier expects a per-CPU allocation. Later operations can then read or write unintended kernel addresses. Ordinary VPS user-namespace capabilities alone do not grant the required BPF authority; explicit delegation is a separate condition. With that authority, privilege escalation and shared-kernel compromise are plausible, but the reviewed upstream report and fix do not establish a complete node-control or cross-VPS exploit on this platform. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel.',
cs='Na zranitelném jádře může program BPF s potřebným přístupem k typovaným mapám a funkcím jádra uložit běžný ukazatel tam, kde verifikátor očekává alokaci pro jednotlivá CPU. Další operace pak mohou číst nebo zapisovat na jiné adresy v jádře. Samotné capabilities v uživatelském jmenném prostoru VPS potřebná oprávnění k BPF neposkytují; výslovná delegace je samostatnou podmínkou. S těmito oprávněními je možné zvýšení práv a napadení sdíleného jádra, ale analyzované upstreamové hlášení a oprava nedokládají úplný postup k ovládnutí node ani zneužití mezi VPS na této platformě. Neúspěšný pokus může shodit sdílené jádro.',impact=['possible','plausible','possible','plausible'],
outcomes='The primary fix explicitly identifies an arbitrary kernel read/write primitive for the plain-allocation confusion, giving strong potential for node control when the privileged program prerequisites are met. This does not prove that ordinary VPS credentials can load that program or that a platform exploit was executed. VPS-root and cross-VPS effects are possible extensions; authority scope is central to the exposure conclusion.'),
'53260':dict(name='PREEMPT_RT TCP request reference-count race',files=['net/ipv4/inet_connection_sock.c'],
primitive='On PREEMPT_RT, reqsk_queue_hash_req can be preempted between arming a timer and initializing rsk_refcnt. Listener closure and timer expiry then perform drops before the references exist, producing underflow/use-after-free. The fix brackets mod_timer and refcount_set with preempt_disable_nested/preempt_enable_nested while keeping mutex-like RT ehash insertion outside that region.',
gates='Necessary CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT is not set in the exact archived .95 configuration; CONFIG_INET=y. This positive configuration evidence excludes that exact build. PREEMPT_DYNAMIC and the full/lazy preemption mode are not PREEMPT_RT and do not make the substituted RT locking path exist. Ordinary tenant TCP listener/connect/close is a potential trigger on a genuinely RT build. Host TCP listeners and network backup/NFS service workloads mean storage is also applicable if such a build was used; role exclusion cannot replace the RT config check.',
current='The .113 reqsk_queue_hash_req protects timer/refcount initialization with the nested preemption pair, matching889fc999. Current source correction and archived non-RT exclusion are separate facts; neither invents historical per-node configuration.',
en='On a kernel built for real-time preemption, closing a TCP listener can race initialization of a connection request and leave the kernel using a freed request. This could support privilege escalation inside a VPS or affect the shared node, although the reviewed upstream report and fix do not establish a complete node-control or cross-VPS exploit. The exact archived vpsAdminOS 6.12.95 build excludes the required real-time mode; that finding applies to this build and does not by itself prove every historical deployment safe. On an affected real-time build, failed attempts may crash the kernel.',
cs='Na jádře sestaveném s real-time preempcí může zavírání naslouchajícího TCP socketu proběhnout souběžně s inicializací požadavku na spojení a jádro pak může používat uvolněný požadavek. Chyba by mohla umožnit zvýšení oprávnění ve VPS nebo ohrozit sdílený node, ale analyzované upstreamové hlášení a oprava nedokládají úplný postup k ovládnutí node ani zneužití mezi VPS. Přesné archivované sestavení vpsAdminOS 6.12.95 požadovaný real-time režim neobsahuje. Tento závěr platí pro dané sestavení a sám o sobě nedokládá bezpečnost všech historických nasazení. Na zranitelném real-time sestavení může neúspěšný pokus shodit jádro.',impact=['possible','possible','possible','plausible'],
roles='Both node and storage are assessed if the necessary RT build is present: tenants can control their TCP sockets, and hosts/storage run genuine TCP listeners for backup/NFS and service workloads. A controlled close/request-timer lifetime is required; ordinary remote traffic alone does not establish reliable control of every step.',
response_en='Linux 6.12 includes the fix starting with 6.12.97. Disabling real-time preemption at build time prevents this specific trigger.',response_cs='Ve větvi Linuxu 6.12 je oprava obsažena od verze 6.12.97. Vypnutí real-time preempce při sestavení zabraňuje tomuto konkrétnímu spuštění chyby.'),
'72069':dict(name='PREEMPT_RT unlock RCU lifetime use-after-free',files=['kernel/locking/spinlock_rt.c'],
primitive='The RT substitutes for spinlock/rwlock released their RCU read-side protection before the actual unlock had finished. A concurrent grace period could free the containing object while the unlock still accesses its lock, yielding a freed-object access/write. The fix moves rcu_read_unlock after the RT unlock operation, retaining migrate_enable ordering.',
gates='CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT is not set in the exact archived .95 build, positively excluding the necessary substituted RT lock implementation in that build. PREEMPT_DYNAMIC/full preemption is not equivalent. On an RT kernel, ordinary filesystem, TCP, NFS or other RCU object-locking workloads can provide paths; no single special tenant device is necessary. Node and storage host workloads are applicable conditionally on the RT build. Exact historical configuration, not absence of a warning, determines a negative claim.',
current='Current .113 rt_spin_unlock, rt_read_unlock and rt_write_unlock place rcu_read_unlock after the underlying unlock, matching1f0d56d3. This source correction is independent of the archived non-RT configuration exclusion.',
en='On a kernel built for real-time preemption, unlocking a protected object can end its lifetime protection too early. Another thread can free the object while the unlock operation is still accessing it. Such corruption could support privilege escalation inside a VPS or affect the shared node, but the reviewed upstream report and fix do not establish a complete node-control or cross-VPS exploit. The exact archived vpsAdminOS 6.12.95 build excludes the required real-time mode; this does not by itself prove every historical deployment safe. Failed attempts on an affected real-time build may crash the kernel.',
cs='Na jádře sestaveném s real-time preempcí může odemykání chráněného objektu příliš brzy ukončit ochranu jeho životnosti. Jiné vlákno pak může objekt uvolnit, zatímco k němu operace odemknutí stále přistupuje. Takové poškození by mohlo umožnit zvýšení oprávnění ve VPS nebo ohrozit sdílený node, ale analyzované upstreamové hlášení a oprava nedokládají úplný postup k ovládnutí node ani zneužití mezi VPS. Přesné archivované sestavení vpsAdminOS 6.12.95 požadovaný real-time režim neobsahuje; to samo o sobě nedokládá bezpečnost všech historických nasazení. Neúspěšný pokus na zranitelném real-time sestavení může shodit jádro.',impact=['possible','possible','possible','plausible'],
roles='Both node and storage are applicable on RT builds. Tenant-driven kernel operations and real host filesystem/TCP/NFS/backup workloads can traverse substituted spin/rw locks and RCU lifetimes. The exact archived build disables RT, but storage role is not excluded merely because it lacks VPSes.',
response_en='Linux 6.12 includes the fix starting with 6.12.101. Disabling real-time preemption at build time prevents this specific trigger.',response_cs='Ve větvi Linuxu 6.12 je oprava obsažena od verze 6.12.101. Vypnutí real-time preempce při sestavení zabraňuje tomuto konkrétnímu spuštění chyby.'),
'98222':dict(name='Encrypted-key datablob length overflow',files=['security/keys/encrypted-keys/encrypted.c','security/keys/key.c'],
primitive='encrypted_key_alloc accumulated multiple string/data lengths into u16 datablob_len and key datalen, truncating the allocation length. __ekey_init then copied a long master-key description into the small payload; the primary KASAN report records a32760-byte slab out-of-bounds write. The fix uses check_add_overflow for both16-bit destinations and kzalloc_flex for the allocation.',
gates='KEYS=y and ENCRYPTED_KEYS=m in the exact archived build. The encrypted_keys type must be registered before ordinary key creation reaches its instantiate/allocate callback. vpsAdminOS disables module autoload by default and does not include encrypted_keys in the default preload list. key_type_lookup searches registered types and returns ENOKEY when missing; it does not request this module. Tenant module loading is blocked by initial-userns privilege and default seccomp. A loaded/registered encrypted_keys module changes this prerequisite, so absence from a preload list is only source-profile evidence, not measured runtime absence. Ordinary keyctl is otherwise permitted and key permissions/LSM apply.',
current='The .113 allocator checks both datablob and total payload overflow and uses kzalloc_flex, matching1e720f63. Runtime module registration is not encoded as an invented evaluator field; older configm alone remains insufficient for safe/exposed certainty.',
en='If the encrypted-key type is available, a VPS process can supply key metadata whose combined length overflows the kernel’s allocation size. The resulting copy can overwrite adjacent kernel memory and makes privilege escalation plausible. This key type is a module omitted from the reviewed default preload list, and ordinary VPS processes cannot load kernel modules; its actual registration must still be checked. The reviewed upstream report and fix do not establish a complete node-control or cross-VPS exploit. Failed attempts may crash the shared kernel.',
cs='Pokud je dostupný typ šifrovaných klíčů, může proces ve VPS zadat metadata klíče, jejichž souhrnná délka způsobí přetečení velikosti alokace v jádře. Následné kopírování může přepsat okolní paměť jádra a umožnit zvýšení oprávnění. Tento typ klíčů je modul, který není v analyzovaném výchozím seznamu předem načítaných modulů, a běžný proces ve VPS nemůže moduly jádra načítat. Jeho skutečnou registraci je přesto nutné ověřit. Analyzované upstreamové hlášení a oprava nedokládají úplný postup k ovládnutí node ani zneužití mezi VPS. Neúspěšný pokus může shodit sdílené jádro.',impact=['plausible','possible','possible','plausible']),
'99999':dict(name='IPv4 checksum metadata header corruption',files=['net/ipv4/ip_output.c','drivers/net/tun.c','net/packet/af_packet.c'],
primitive='Untrusted partial-checksum metadata can place checksum_start before the end of a validated IPv4 header. Deferred checksum completion can then rewrite that header after earlier parsing, leading to unsafe downstream interpretation and kernel memory exposure/corruption. The stable32a8b0ad correction introduces ip_check_csum_start and checks before checksum completion in IPv4 fragmentation, bridge/queue/checksum/XFRM paths. Primary text calls fuller input validation forthcoming: this dossier credits the actual corrective commit, not an invented complete metadata-validation redesign.',
gates='CONFIG_INET=y in the archived build. Default TUN feature delegation gives tenant /dev/net/tun with namespace CAP_NET_ADMIN to create/configure TUN/TAP; AF_PACKET is an alternative with namespace CAP_NET_RAW, preloaded af_packet and virtual-network-header/offload metadata. Default seccomp does not deny those operations. CONFIG_TUN or CONFIG_PACKET alone is not listed as necessary because the two paths are alternatives; requiring both would incorrectly exclude one. Crafted checksum metadata is necessary; ordinary unmodified IP traffic is not sufficient. Actual device/features and network/MTU/fragmentation/offload path remain runtime prerequisites.',
current='The .113 ip_do_fragment validates checksum_start via ip_check_csum_start before skb_checksum_help, matching32a8b0ad; the full stable patch also covers bridge/netfilter/XFRM call sites. Both TUN and AF_PACKET source paths were checked against the delegated namespace capability boundary.',
en='A VPS administrator can supply specially crafted checksum metadata through an available TUN/TAP or packet-socket path. Deferred checksum processing can then alter an IPv4 header after validation and lead to kernel memory disclosure or corruption. External research demonstrated memory leakage and host compromise in other KVM and Firecracker setups. That result is serious evidence of the bug’s potential, but it does not demonstrate the same exploit on vpsAdminOS. Root escalation inside a VPS, node compromise and cross-VPS exposure remain plausible consequences of a successful platform-specific exploit; failed attempts can crash the shared node.',
cs='Správce VPS může přes dostupné rozhraní TUN/TAP nebo paketový socket dodat speciálně upravená metadata kontrolního součtu. Odložené zpracování součtu pak může změnit hlavičku IPv4 až po její kontrole a způsobit únik nebo poškození paměti jádra. Externí výzkum předvedl únik paměti a napadení hostitele v jiných konfiguracích KVM a Firecracker. Jde o závažný doklad možných dopadů chyby, nikoli o předvedení stejného zneužití na vpsAdminOS. Zvýšení oprávnění ve VPS, napadení node a ohrožení jiného VPS jsou reálné možné důsledky úspěšného zneužití přizpůsobeného této platformě. Neúspěšné pokusy mohou shodit sdílený node.',impact=['plausible','plausible','plausible','plausible'],
outcomes='The CNA links [PWNAI PwnEscape](https://pwn.ai/blog/pwnescape) and [Vercel challenge report](https://vercel.com/blog/findings-from-the-1-million-dollar-vercel-sandbox-challenge), both retrieved2026-10-19 and inspected. Vercel distinguishes host-memory leakage demonstrated against its production sandbox from crashes/full administrator command execution demonstrated on the researcher own KVM/Firecracker machines matching its configuration. PWNAI likewise claims a full guest-to-host escape but reserves the full primitive-to-control account for later work. This is demonstrated external exploitation, not a reproduced vpsAdminOS/container exploit. On this platform, delegated TUN/AF_PACKET gives source-backed access to the vulnerable metadata surface, making node and cross-VPS consequences plausible; exact exploit success is not established.' )})
